-- title:
--   Automorphism fixing all n-th roots of a finite set is trivial
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ and $L$ be fields with $L$ a $K$-algebra, let $n$ be a natural number, and let $S$ be a finite set of units of $K$. Assume $L$ is a splitting field over $K$ of the polynomial $\prod_{u \in S} (X^n - u)$, where each $u \in S$ is regarded as an element of $K$ via the coercion from $K^\times$; that is, this polynomial splits over $L$ and $L$ is generated over $K$ by its roots. Let $\sigma$ be a $K$-algebra automorphism of $L$ with the property that $\sigma(\alpha) = \alpha$ for every $\alpha \in L$ such that $\alpha^n = u$ in $L$ (with $u$ transported along $\mathrm{algebraMap}\, K\, L$) for at least one $u \in S$. The conclusion is that $\sigma$ is the identity automorphism of $L$. No hypothesis is imposed on $n$ (it may be $0$), on the characteristic of $K$, or on the presence of $n$-th roots of unity in $K$.
--
--   This is the non-degeneracy, on the Galois side, of the Kummer pairing for the subgroup of $K^\times$ generated by $S$: a Galois element acting trivially on all the chosen radicals is trivial. It is used in the determination of the relevant power subgroup as the subgroup generated by $S$ together with $n$-th powers, [`KummerTheory.powerSubgroup_eq_closure_sup_range_of_isSplittingField`](thm.html#KummerTheory.powerSubgroup_eq_closure_sup_range_of_isSplittingField), and in a norm-index estimate for number fields in the presence of primitive roots of unity.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_KummerTheory_algEquiv_eq_one_of_forall_apply_eq_of_isSplittingField.lean

